From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DeepSeek Harness <noreply@deepseek.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 10:59:10 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(app): merge Rime dictionaries from adb and repair
 sync_dir

The Syncthing bridge only copied non-dictionary files, and a profile reset
could drop sync_dir from installation.yaml, after which librime silently
synced into the app-private rime/sync directory instead of the shared
folder.

* RimeProfileSync restores a missing sync_dir before comparing the staged
  profile, so the shared folder is used again even after a fresh install.
* RimeImportReceiver gains RIME_SYNC, which runs librime's
  sync_user_data() through the Rime addon "sync" sub-config (the same path
  as the schema-menu "Synchronize" item) without a visible keyboard.
* RIME_IMPORT now merges dictionaries after applying the profile, so
  *.userdb.txt staged next to the config files is picked up too.
* tools/: PC push/pull script and a systemd user timer to drive both
  actions over adb.

Built as 0.1.3-patchwork / 11205 (PATCHWORK_REVISION=5).
